      {
        "Id": "49082c9845b44eba98bc9de2ad3ee4c4",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  0 = which views: SELECTED (click views in the Project Browser, Ctrl = more), ACTIVE, or words in the view names (comma list).  1 = sub-discipline: LIGHTING, POWER, FIRE ALARM, ELV, HVAC, MECHANICAL, VENTILATION, PLUMBING, DRAINAGE, FIRE FIGHTING, STRUCTURAL, INTERIOR, COORDINATION, or your own word (then set 2).  2 = AUTO picks the discipline (Lighting > Electrical, HVAC > Mechanical, Fire Fighting > Plumbing) or type ARCHITECTURAL / STRUCTURAL / MECHANICAL / ELECTRICAL / PLUMBING / COORDINATION.  3 = ASSIGN files the views, COPY duplicates each view once per sub-discipline in 1 (comma list, e.g. LIGHTING, HVAC, PLUMBING, FIRE, or PROJECT = every sub-discipline in 5), CLEAR empties Sub-Discipline, LIST shows every view by Discipline > Sub-Discipline.  4 = name of copies.  5 = THIS PROJECT's sub-disciplines, e.g. LIGHTING, POWER, HVAC, PLUMBING - saved in the project on the first RUN = True, then leave blank; others are refused; ALL = no limit.  6 RUN False = preview, True = change.  Adds the Sub-Discipline view parameter if missing.  PROJECT BROWSER: on RUN = True the script adds the scheme \"SD Discipline\" (Discipline > Sub-Discipline) and switches to it by itself - the Browser Organization window opens and closes on its own.",
        "DescriptionText": "",
